# 13. Create Neural Network

Now we use PyTorch's `nn.Module`.

```python
class NeuralNetwork(nn.Module):

    def __init__(self, input_size):
        super().__init__()

        self.layer1 = nn.Linear(input_size, 8)
        self.relu = nn.ReLU()

        self.layer2 = nn.Linear(8, 1)
        self.sigmoid = nn.Sigmoid()

    def forward(self, X):

        z1 = self.layer1(X)

        h1 = self.relu(z1)

        z2 = self.layer2(h1)

        yp = self.sigmoid(z2)

        return yp
```

Architecture:

```text
6 Input Features
       ↓
nn.Linear(6, 8)
       ↓
8 Hidden Neurons
       ↓
     ReLU
       ↓
nn.Linear(8, 1)
       ↓
    Sigmoid
       ↓
1 Prediction
```

---

# 14. Understanding nn.Linear

Previously we manually wrote:

```python
z1 = X @ w1 + b1
```

Now:

```python
z1 = self.layer1(X)
```

does essentially the same operation.

```text
nn.Linear
   ↓
automatically manages
   ↓
Weights + Bias
```

Therefore we don't manually create:

```text
w1
b1
w2
b2
```

