# 28. Manual vs PyTorch nn

What we previously did manually:

```text
Manual                           PyTorch

w1, b1                      →    nn.Linear()
w2, b2                      →    nn.Linear()

X @ w1 + b1                 →    layer1(X)

manual ReLU                 →    nn.ReLU()

manual Sigmoid              →    nn.Sigmoid()

manual loss                 →    nn.BCELoss()

loss.backward()             →    loss.backward()

w -= lr * w.grad            →    optimizer.step()

w.grad.zero_()              →    optimizer.zero_grad()
```

So PyTorch is not doing a completely different algorithm.

It is automating the same concepts we learned manually.

